{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RA", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\cite[IV, Definition 11.10.2]{EGA}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:333938e8330f1d3604d493fbe58201f9e37d5237454cbda562e7352799e97cf5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe take the following definition from <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c69291dc4f59b2265c4ad3624d63ea0850f1193f0f6faacd48fd699aa2e8ebfc", "unit_id": "tag:01RA:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01RA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$V \\subset X$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\cap V$", "MATH_0010": "$V$", "MATH_0011": "$V$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-scheme-theoretically-dense}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e3c7760ded8aba9fdf27a9fd5d8c65cd74541f82c7419fd431ab27d83fd35918", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:72a29a0adfbc608c1d706f0a2818d2e9c558eee10ebcc0e7bd37b92f2338939c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an open subscheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme theoretic image of the morphism <MATH_0003>\nis called the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>scheme theoretic closure of <MATH_0004> in <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0006> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>scheme theoretically dense in <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif for every open <MATH_0008> the scheme theoretic closure\nof <MATH_0009> in <MATH_0010> is equal to <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a0e93e642d313f0db8624afb4c3fa666caf35c6e0a772f79b74e7859634f13ff", "unit_id": "tag:01RB:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01RA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$V \\subset X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(U \\cap V)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-scheme-theretically-dense-not-dense}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-scheme-theoretically-dense-quasi-compact}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-reduced-scheme-theoretically-dense}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-characterize-scheme-theoretically-dense}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTBFCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTBFOPEN_0001": "{\\bf "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d7d58394f4d584de1322d0fa2d33bbfabd15a07da8f856a9d2bd9214c7636b2c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c12e4ca1bfe33fd7192d4c26c8751fd6275c95d90b50704bc7d6b4134acaf0ca", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWith this definition it is\n<TEXTBFOPEN_0001>not<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> the case that <MATH_0001> is scheme theoretically dense in <MATH_0002> if and\nonly if the scheme theoretic closure of <MATH_0003> is <MATH_0004>, see\nExample <REF_0001>.\nThis is somewhat inelegant; but see\nLemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>\nbelow. On the other hand, with this definition <MATH_0005> is scheme theoretically\ndense in <MATH_0006> if and only if for every <MATH_0007> open the ring map\n<MATH_0008> is injective, see\nLemma <REF_0004>\nbelow. In particular we see that scheme theoretically dense implies dense\nwhich is pleasing.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b276c9c5dc5bd756dea0fe9524044f48ae07a7d6d7795082e98dc26617678b02", "unit_id": "tag:01RA:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "01RA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$k$", "MATH_0003": "$A = k[x, z_1, z_2, \\ldots]/(x^n z_n)$", "MATH_0004": "$I = (z_1, z_2, \\ldots) \\subset A$", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0006": "$U = X \\setminus V(I)$", "MATH_0007": "$A \\to \\prod_n A_{z_n}$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$X \\to \\Spec(k[x])$", "MATH_0011": "$z_n = 0$", "MATH_0012": "$U$", "MATH_0013": "$x = 0$", "MATH_0014": "$U$", "MATH_0015": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-scheme-theretically-dense-not-dense}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c499149846398f62a21337f36e919c933cf9e7d3e942717920681be14274f5ba", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8c50da5da43512c82f3e88675a4ac77b3458f00e19e63056b5e8fa878de871f5", "source_text": "Here is an example where scheme theoretic closure being <MATH_0001> does not\nimply dense for the underlying topological spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a field.\nSet <MATH_0003>\nSet <MATH_0004>.\nConsider the affine scheme <MATH_0005> and the\nopen subscheme <MATH_0006>.\nSince <MATH_0007> is injective we see that the scheme theoretic\nclosure of <MATH_0008> is <MATH_0009>. Consider the morphism\n<MATH_0010>. This morphism is surjective\n(set all <MATH_0011> to see this). But the restriction\nof this morphism to <MATH_0012> is not surjective because it maps\nto the point <MATH_0013>. Hence <MATH_0014> cannot be topologically dense\nin <MATH_0015>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:99e9c0b2d1fa79d4a9b86aa4844e464a068bbee0555e3dc9978de81941158bdb", "unit_id": "tag:01RC:statement"}
